WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:17.164
"Let's go after Maggie whispered.

2
00:00:18.265 --> 00:00:19.585
She sounded excited now.

3
00:00:20.605 --> 00:00:21.926
"She's almost reached the woods!"

4
00:00:21.946 --> 00:00:26.147
"No, let's wait for a few seconds," Henry said.

5
00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:29.168
"We don't want her to hear us following her."

6
00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:32.945
He watched Nora until she disappeared into the woods.

7
00:00:34.706 --> 00:00:38.488
A few seconds later there was a glow from just inside the tree line.

8
00:00:38.508 --> 00:00:42.410
"It looks like she brought a flashlight," Cole said.

9
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.171
Henry nodded.

10
00:00:44.191 --> 00:00:47.232
"That should make it a lot easier to spot her.

11
00:00:48.212 --> 00:00:50.313
Come on, I think it's safe to climb down now.

12
00:00:51.254 --> 00:00:52.534
She's too far away to hear us."

13
00:00:53.535 --> 00:00:55.596
He led the way down from the tree house.

14
00:00:56.992 --> 00:00:59.894
The three detectives hurried across the yard toward the woods.

15
00:00:59.914 --> 00:01:05.897
"It's getting kind of dark," Maggie said, peering at the trail that led into the forest.

16
00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:08.478
"I hope we'll be able to see."

17
00:01:08.498 --> 00:01:10.119
"Don't worry.

18
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.421
I brought a flashlight too."

19
00:01:13.421 --> 00:01:14.342
Henry pulled it out.

20
00:01:15.382 --> 00:01:17.023
He stepped onto the shadowy trail.

21
00:01:18.384 --> 00:01:21.245
It was time to put step three of his plan into action.

22
00:01:22.286 --> 00:01:25.728
Henry waited a second longer, and then turned on his flashlight.

23
00:01:26.796 --> 00:01:31.259
He shined it around until he found the flour that he and Cole had sprinkled on the ground

24
00:01:31.379 --> 00:01:32.160
earlier that day.

25
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.842
"Wow," Maggie said.

26
00:01:34.862 --> 00:01:37.744
"You guys sure used a lot of flour."

27
00:01:41.026 --> 00:01:41.767
Cole grinned.

28
00:01:41.787 --> 00:01:43.949
"We used the whole bag.

29
00:01:44.949 --> 00:01:47.831
I hope Nathan's parents don't decide to bake a cake anytime soon."

30
00:01:47.851 --> 00:01:53.876
"Using a lot of flour was the only way my plan would work," Henry explained to Maggie.

31
00:01:54.912 --> 00:01:59.116
"We had to sprinkle enough on the ground so that Nora would be sure to step in it."

32
00:02:00.437 --> 00:02:01.178
Cole nodded.

33
00:02:01.198 --> 00:02:05.202
"Now all we have to do is follow her footprints," he said.

34
00:02:05.222 --> 00:02:10.267
"I always knew Henry was smart, but this has to be the coolest plan ever!"

35
00:02:10.287 --> 00:02:15.992
"I hope Nora didn't see the flour and jump over it," Maggie said, worried.

36
00:02:16.012 --> 00:02:19.436
"I thought about that," Henry said.

37
00:02:20.636 --> 00:02:25.257
"That's why we made sure to put it here in the woods, under the trees, instead of out

38
00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:25.858
in the yard.

39
00:02:27.018 --> 00:02:29.759
It gets dark here a lot sooner than it does out there."

40
00:02:29.779 --> 00:02:31.739
"Good thinking!"

41
00:02:32.139 --> 00:02:33.179
Maggie was impressed.

42
00:02:33.199 --> 00:02:36.480
"Nora didn't turn on her flashlight right away.

43
00:02:37.561 --> 00:02:39.381
So she probably didn't see the flour."

44
00:02:40.802 --> 00:02:41.522
Cole grinned.

45
00:02:41.542 --> 00:02:44.162
"That's what we were hoping she'd do."

46
00:02:45.243 --> 00:02:48.364
Henry was shining his flashlight up and down the line of flour.

47
00:02:48.384 --> 00:02:54.270
"There!" he cried, spotting some powdery, white footprints leading deeper into the woods.

48
00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.651
They had to be Nora's!

49
00:02:57.791 --> 00:03:01.013
He followed the footprints, keeping his flashlight aimed at the ground.

50
00:03:02.633 --> 00:03:04.394
His friends crept along behind him.

51
00:03:04.414 --> 00:03:09.156
"The footprints are getting fainter already," Maggie whispered.

52
00:03:09.176 --> 00:03:13.818
"I guess it didn't take long for most of the flour to come off Nora's shoes.

53
00:03:14.899 --> 00:03:17.400
What if the footprints run out before we catch up to her?"

54
00:03:18.536 --> 00:03:23.119
"If that happens, at least we'll know what direction she's going," Henry whispered back.

55
00:03:23.139 --> 00:03:29.322
"And it's definitely not toward that shed where she pretended she was going before," Cole added.

56
00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:32.984
"It's a good thing that Henry was too smart to fall for that!"

57
00:03:33.004 --> 00:03:36.046
"Are you saying I wasn't smart enough?"

58
00:03:36.526 --> 00:03:38.247
Maggie asked, sounding insulted.

59
00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.748
"Shh!" Henry hushed them.

60
00:03:40.768 --> 00:03:43.630
"I don't want her to hear us coming!"

61
00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.832
Maggie and Cole stayed quiet after that.

62
00:03:47.808 --> 00:03:52.072
The three friends tiptoed through the woods, following the faint flour footprints.

63
00:03:53.273 --> 00:03:56.415
It was getting so dark that the woods seemed a little spooky.

64
00:03:57.536 --> 00:04:02.460
Insects and frogs chirped all around the kids, and an owl hooted in the distance.

65
00:04:04.041 --> 00:04:06.123
But Henry stayed focused on the footprints.

66
00:04:07.204 --> 00:04:08.986
They were getting fainter and fainter.

67
00:04:10.126 --> 00:04:12.188
Finally they disappeared completely.

68
00:04:12.208 --> 00:04:14.530
"Uh-oh," Cole whispered.

69
00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.572
"It's the end of the trail!"

70
00:04:17.632 --> 00:04:20.074
Henry turned off his flashlight and looked around.

71
00:04:21.135 --> 00:04:23.076
It was hard to see anything in the darkness.

72
00:04:24.177 --> 00:04:26.819
But then he saw something up ahead—a light!

73
00:04:26.839 --> 00:04:29.741
"Look!" he whispered.

74
00:04:29.761 --> 00:04:32.643
"That must be Nora's flashlight."

75
00:04:33.784 --> 00:04:34.804
"Let's go get her!"

76
00:04:35.165 --> 00:04:36.365
Maggie whispered eagerly.

77
00:04:37.446 --> 00:04:41.229
The three of them hurried toward the light, moving as quietly as they could.

78
00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.192
Henry was in the lead as they emerged into a clearing.

79
00:04:46.708 --> 00:04:48.869
On the far side was a huge oak tree.

80
00:04:49.909 --> 00:04:51.709
The light was coming from the base of the tree.

81
00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.490
Nora was there, leaning over.

82
00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:57.031
Her back was to the detectives.

83
00:04:58.151 --> 00:04:59.912
She hadn't heard or seen them yet.

84
00:05:00.952 --> 00:05:04.293
Henry squinted, trying to see what she was doing, but he couldn't tell.

85
00:05:05.673 --> 00:05:09.914
He was about to whisper to his friends that they should hide behind the trees and watch Nora.

86
00:05:10.894 --> 00:05:12.955
But Maggie was already pushing past him.

87
00:05:12.975 --> 00:05:15.036
"Freeze, Nora!"

88
00:05:15.476 --> 00:05:16.276
she said loudly.

89
00:05:17.428 --> 00:05:18.230
"We caught you!"

90
00:05:19.332 --> 00:05:22.199
Nora spun around and gasped.

91
00:05:22.299 --> 00:05:22.680
"Oh no!"

92
00:05:23.101 --> 00:05:24.243
she cried in surprise.
